Action: run_sql({'query': "SELECT e.name, r.rating, r.text\nFROM review r\nJOIN establishments e ON r.gmap_id = e.gmap_id\nWHERE (e.address LIKE '%84116%' OR e.address LIKE '%Rose Park%')\n  AND ST_Y(e.geom) BETWEEN 40.768 AND 40.805\n  AND ST_X(e.geom) BETWEEN -111.95 AND -111.91\n  AND (\n    LOWER(r.text) LIKE '%breakfast%'\n    OR LOWER(r.text) LIKE '%egg%'\n    OR LOWER(r.text) LIKE '%burrito%'\n    OR LOWER(r.text) LIKE '%chilaquiles%'\n    OR LOWER(r.text) LIKE '%menudo%'\n    OR LOWER(r.text) LIKE '%tamale%'\n    OR LOWER(r.text) LIKE '%savory%'\n  )\nORDER BY e.avg_rating DESC, e.num_of_reviews DESC\nLIMIT 100;"})

Observation: {"row_count": 100, "truncated": true, "rows": [{"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "This is a total hidden gem. They've got a lot of vegetarian options, but some meat dishes too so don't let that scare you away if veggie isn't your thing. We ordered spring rolls, BBQ noodle salad, and lemongrass fried rice, and it was all amazing."}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 2.0, "text": "My fiance and I have been going here since we started eating plant based (3 years) and we always enjoyed the food. I am sad to say that the past few times we have been disappointed. We got the teriyaki banh mi a few weeks ago, and they didn't add the faux meat, which is where most of the flavor is! Today, we got takeout and it was the most disappointing meal we've had. Everything tasted entirely different (and not in a good way). We ordered 2 of the pho with extra veggies and didn't get the extra veggies. We ordered the all chay egg rolls which were decent, but again, entirely different from the amazing flavor they normally have. We had 2 orders of Thai tea w/popping boba and it was EXTREMELY watered down and we couldn't even taste the tea. The only good part of the Thai tea was the popping boba. My fiance also had an All Chay banh mi and the bread was extremely difficult to eat; almost a chewy, rubbery texture. He didn't end up finishing his pho because it didn't taste good and his stomach really started hurting. I'm leaving a rating of 2 stars instead of 1 because they have great customer service. However, we were very disappointed about the meal and our most recent experiences. They have also increased the pricing of everything, so our meal today was almost $50 and honestly wasn't worth one cent. I hate to leave such a harsh rating, but we frequently eat here (this used to be our favorite restaurant!) and when we don't get everything we pay for and the flavor has really been lacking, I will speak up. I can honestly say that we probably won't be back for a while because it doesn't taste like love is being poured into the food, if you know what I mean. We just hope that if we do decide to come back in the future, that our experience won't be that of today's."}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "Food is great. I want to congratulate this place for having the most kind and friendly man at the cashier (might be the owner). He will always greet you with a big smile and help you as much as he can. This is a comfort pho, and other Vietnamese-Asian dishes. I believe everything here in Vegan. I would love to see more veggies and noodles in the pho, but other than that the flavor is amazing!"}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "Curry Rice and All Chai Egg Roles"}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "I love Vietnamese food and now there's a place to get it vegan! I LOVED the shrimp on noodle dish, the egg rolls, all season rolls, banh mi, pho, and thai tea. We went back two days later because it was so good. I couldn't recommend this place more highly."}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "Love everything I\u2019ve gotten here! All vegan. My go-to\u2019s are the lemongrass fried rice and the pho. The veggie rolls are awesome too \ud83e\udd70"}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "Good location for delicious Vietnamese food. The food was so savory. Had a friend come into town and asked me to take him here again. Feels similar to a restaurant in New York I loved."}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "I stopped here during a trip to Salt Lake and I wish I didn\u2019t have to leave just so I could eat here more often! I got the egg rolls, \u201cshrimp\u201d, and pho. All delicious!!"}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "Amazing place with such amazingly delicious food, the shrimp will fool anyone with how accurate the flavor and texture was and those egg rolls are incredible, also the chicken nuggets,the bon mi was so delicious aswell and the people that either work there or own it was so sweet and kind!!!"}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "DELICIOUS! I got the hu tieu and the veggie meats and broth were yum and rich in flavor. Drumsticks are yummy (not on menu), but if you order it, you can have it! One order has two of them. All Chay eggless rolls are perfectly fried and tasty. They are oily though, of course, as they are fried. By the way chay means vegetarian in Vietnamese. Being Vietnamese and not eating meat anymore, it's a great to taste authentic and yummy Vietnamese food with a vegan twist. Recommended highly!!"}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 4.0, "text": "Vegetarian restaurant, the tofu lemongrass is really good the \"egg roll\" is a good egg roll regardless of being vegetarian."}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "I fall into the not vegan but still love this place category. Every time I go I try something new, and each time it is absolutely delicious. The nuggets are great, the egg rolls are great, the pho is great, the noodles are great. The different vegan 'meats' are all tasty, as is the straight tofu.\n\nThe people working there are also super friendly and nice to talk to, and I always have a good time no matter what.\n\nIf every vegan place had food this good I would have no qualms about going vegan whatsoever. I just wish they were open on Monday so I had the option every day of the week."}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "Awesome place. Truly a hidden gem. The staff is incredibly nice and the food is on point. Love the All Chay egg rolls."}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "All Chay is the best food I've ever had.  Love this place!  Try the lemongrass rice or the pho.  Or the All Chay egg rolls.  Or everything.\n."}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "The egg rolls here are amazing. I also like their teraki rice dish. The workers are fantastic as well. They're always so polite."}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "I love this place and it's sister restaurant vegan bowl. Amaizing place to get pho and egg rolls!"}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "I can't believe this place isn't more packed than it is every time I go. Honestly, I'm glad Rose Park is the location for this establishment. Besides all the fast food and cheap Mexican on this part of town I am glad there's a delicious alternative.\n\nI recommend the Ocean Love Noodles! It's my go to meal every time I go. It has breaded \"shrimp\" and lots and lots of veggies over noodles.\n\nThe owners are (brother & sister) and they are wonderful people."}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "I was here for dinner last night. It appears family run business and very friendly staff.\nCounter service and sit wherever you like.\n\nI ordered Mongolian noodle salad(beef, noodle,egg rolls and salad) with  rice paper rolls aside. Meals came quick.\n\nFish sauce for the salad was really good. It made the meal very tasty.\n\nNothing fancy about it,but if you like eating. Recommend!"}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "Flavorful and filling from savory noodles and tasty rice dishes to delicious desserts even your non vegan/vegetarian friends will love it!"}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "Food here is amazing and super cheap <3 got a Bahmi sandwich, the ocean lovers noodles and egg rolls. Every thing was cooked to perfection and the staff is so friendly. Wish I lived around here cause I\u2019d go here all the time. Al Chay for the win \ud83e\udd18"}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "Today I got up early and went fly fishing. It was pretty cold, and when I was done I really wanted some kind of spicy soup. Normally, I would seek out a Mexican joint and a bowl of menudo or posole. This time I opted for some Pho, and I have zero regrets. It was delicious and satisfying. I used the house chili sauce to spice my pho at the table, phew that stuff has plenty of kick! Despite my wide eyes and runny nose, I polished off the bowl. The service here is excellent. Perhaps my only complaint was the weird chimey music that was playing on loop."}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "All Chay has been one of my favorite vegan restaurants for about a year now. They always deliver great food and usually the wait time is only about 5 to 7 minutes. I really love their rice dishes and the all chay eggrolls but I havent been disappointed with anything on their menu and any family or friends I have brought with me, vegan or not, are always impressed with flavor and the amount of food provided. 10/10."}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "Since going vegan, I have definitely noticed that were limited to about 6 restaurants. Out of all of them, this is my ultimate favorite. They have the best \"egg\" rolls I've ever had and I love their teriaki \"chicken\" dish with rice. They are also very kind. Seems like a family business. Yesterday, they were closed when i showed up but they let us order anyway. I'm about to go in to try something new..... at my seriously favorite place to eat :)"}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "Veggie House is hands-down the best vegan spot in SLC. They have amazing food, a super relaxed environment, and they're very helpful! I try to go at least once a week :)"}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "Fills the body and soul.  Vegetarian greatness in pho, bahn mi, egg rolls, and more.  New Year's Day recovery meal could not have been better!"}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "The food here is amazing. We love the \"Ocean Love Noodle Bowl\" and the \"All Chay Eggrolls\". I think the place is family owned and run, and they are the sweetest people. One day I called them one minute after closing and they were still happy to prep my order because they hadn't put all the food away. They give some of the best service I have every received at a restaurant."}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "This place is AMAZING! I am Vietnamese and grew up with my mom making Pho right at home. When I became vegan my mom suggested this place since I was craving Pho really bad about 2 months in.\n\nWe order the Pho, and I couldn't believe the broth was vegan! I couldn't believe the plant based beef wasn't beef! The broth was spot on and I am so glad I found this place so I can get my Pho fix! They have great eggrolls, don't get the veggie ones get the other ones that only give you the 4 vs the 5! It is worth it, trust me! Love this place! \u2665\ufe0f\u2665\ufe0f\u2665\ufe0f"}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "The best vegan egg rolls! I love this place!"}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "Really nice folks, quiet, and peaceful with no hipster vibe. The best pho I've ever had. I have other favorite places, but this one has everything right. Fantastic egg rolls"}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "Undeniably delectable. Took my nonvegan mom here and she loved everything we tried. \"I cant even choose which thing i liked best, all of them were too dang good!\" Her words :). But I know my favorites were the fried rice, egg rolls ( these are PERFECT, you would NOT be able to tell the difference between these & nonvegan eggrolls), fried shrimp and the pho! Will be coming back again and again, cant wait to try every last plate on the menu! Yummy carrot juice too. (:"}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "I had such a great dinner here tonight! I ordered the Golden Noodle and my gal ordered the Mongolian beef as a rice dish instead of noodle. Both dishes were very good. The egg rolls are seriously THE BEST I've ever had. The counter service was an added touch, being able to eat and not be interrupted so it gives some privacy which I love. There's a condiment and utensil station set up in the middle so you're able to get whatever you'd need. I'll definitely be returning!"}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "My pho and egg rolls were fantastic!"}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "Fills the body and soul.  Vegetarian greatness in pho, bahn mi, egg rolls, and more.  New Year's Day recovery meal could not have been better!"}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "The full menu is vegan, but your non-veggie friends will never notice. I've vistited several times now and have yet to find anything on the menu that wasn't delicious. The environment is very peaceful and relaxing--a great place to dine alone or with friends."}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "They have the best vegan options I have found! Their eggrolls are a must when you go. We usually get the pho or the teriyaki \"chicken\" which is delicious. We drive up from Ogden just for their food. Never have had a bad experience!"}, {"name": "All Chay", "rating": 5.0, "text": "I'm not a vegan. I don't know what right, spell, potion, or incantation one must recite to be one of those... Yet, this place does have vegan offerings. Folks who are in the know on vegan protocol will have to judge that.\n\nI'll stick with taste, quality, service, and price.\n\nIt was all great. When you do finally get here go ahead and meander up to the counter and order your goodies. No need to wait to be seated.\n\nI got the pho and it was great. My wife even liked it and she isn't a pho fiend like me.\n\nThere are some egg rolls on here I can't wait to get back and try. Nothing like the ones in the pic.\n\nOnce you've eaten your goodies please make sure you clean up after yourself. They have dish buckets by the water coolers in the center of the room. Dump your food and plan your next trip back."}, {"name": "El Jaripeo Taco Truck (Rose Park)", "rating": 5.0, "text": "This place is BOMB! Y\u2019all I love cetos aka betos and never thought no burritos or tacos could beat it. But I was wrong this food truck knows E X A C T L Y what they\u2019re doing. Just go and try it!!"}, {"name": "El Jaripeo Taco Truck (Rose Park)", "rating": 5.0, "text": "These guys know what they're doing. Found them from a pic someone posted to Reddit and I'm so glad I did. Burrito was huge, delicious and reasonably priced. Definitely coming back for the nachos next time"}, {"name": "El Jaripeo Taco Truck (Rose Park)", "rating": 5.0, "text": "Everything is good here tacos,tortas and burritos. The truck is in the Smith's parking lot."}, {"name": "Tacos Do\u00f1a Mary L.L.C.", "rating": 5.0, "text": "This taco stand has high quality food. A burrito is $4.50 and tacos are around $1.  You can put pico de gio on it as well."}, {"name": "Tacos Do\u00f1a Mary L.L.C.", "rating": 5.0, "text": "I had the pastor burrito with red salsa and it was very tasty. Can't wait to go back and try some more burritos and tacos."}, {"name": "Tacos Do\u00f1a Mary L.L.C.", "rating": 5.0, "text": "Excellent tacos ($1.50), burritos ($5.50), and quesadillas for reasonable prices."}, {"name": "Tacos Do\u00f1a Mary L.L.C.", "rating": 5.0, "text": "Great burritos"}, {"name": "Tacos Do\u00f1a Mary L.L.C.", "rating": 5.0, "text": "Always good food. My favorite is the  Chile-verda burrito. Green Chile and cactus. Good stuff."}, {"name": "Tacos Do\u00f1a Mary L.L.C.", "rating": 5.0, "text": "Great little taco trailer amongst franchise giants. Lots of parking and the food is made to order.  For you truck drivers at Loves it\u2019s a short walk and it beats fast food any day.  Street tacos, burritos and a thicker version of masa dough flattened out and topped with your choice of meats and all the fresh fixings your salivating mouth can handle.  The Hispanic lady does her best to keep the line moving.  Be patient because good food takes time.  Not greasy, but fresh ingredients paired with Ice cold soft drinks (pop).  I know I\u2019ll walk my tubby butt over when I\u2019m in town!"}, {"name": "Tacos Do\u00f1a Mary L.L.C.", "rating": 5.0, "text": "Awesome food truck. The asada burrito was very good."}, {"name": "Red Iguana", "rating": 5.0, "text": "Oh man, this was my favorite place to eat when my sister lived out in Salt Lake. We would order a mole platter (and you must order the mole; it's incredible!) and I would get a mango margarita (say what you will. I like what I like.). It was a feast that could satisfy anyone. Savory food, a cool atmosphere, and some tasty beverages. Yes, there is usually a wait. It is well worth it."}, {"name": "Red Iguana", "rating": 3.0, "text": "Eh, I was underwhelmed. The food was decent, but I've definitely had better. I guess this is good for Salt Lake City. We ordered the Chile Rellenos and Chile Verde Burritos. The chile rellenos were soggy and covered in a red sauce that I didn't care much for. Would have been better with just the chile and a little bit of crema mexicana. The pork in the chile verde burritos were tough and drenched in a green sauce which I also didn't care for. I don't think this place warranted the 35 minute wait."}, {"name": "Red Iguana", "rating": 4.0, "text": "There is a reason Red Iguana is continually rated one of the best Mexican food eateries in Utah.  Can\u2019t beat the guac and the carne asada burritos are near perfection.  Love the comfy cozy authentic environment."}, {"name": "Red Iguana", "rating": 4.0, "text": "Better than average, good service, nice atmosphere, and great selection. No Tamales during the week. So keep that in mind.  There are plenty of things to drink, and a fine dessert menu as well. Remember they offer large portions."}]}

Action: run_sql({'query': "SELECT e.gmap_id, e.name, e.address, e.avg_rating, e.num_of_reviews, e.price,\n       MIN(gh.open_min) as earliest_open_min,\n       STRING_AGG(DISTINCT c.category, ', ') as categories\nFROM establishments e\nLEFT JOIN gmap_hours gh ON e.gmap_id = gh.gmap_id\nLEFT JOIN establishment_categories ec ON e.gmap_id = ec.gmap_id\nLEFT JOIN category c ON ec.category_id = c.category_id\nWHERE (e.address LIKE '%84116%' OR e.address LIKE '%Rose Park%')\n  AND ST_Y(e.geom) BETWEEN 40.768 AND 40.805\n  AND ST_X(e.geom) BETWEEN -111.95 AND -111.91\nGROUP BY e.gmap_id, e.name, e.address, e.avg_rating, e.num_of_reviews, e.price\nHAVING MIN(gh.open_min) IS NOT NULL AND MIN(gh.open_min) <= 600 -- 10:00 AM is 600 minutes\nORDER BY e.avg_rating DESC, e.num_of_reviews DESC;"})

